node_modules/
# `lib/` is deliberately committed (see README「构建产物与漂移校验」): a Git-spec
# install never runs a build and ships only this subdirectory, so the built
# artifacts — including the bundled Connector at `lib/connector/` — must be in
# the repository. `yarn check:build` guards them against drift.
.drift-check/
.yarn/
.pnp.*
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
*.tgz
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Legacy junk, never to return: an older commands test passed a *relative*
# `dataDir`, so `runAutoLogin` wrote `login.json` into this package directory
# (`opencode-plugin/unused/login.json`) and it got committed. The test now uses
# a temp dir; this line keeps any future mistake out of the history.
unused/
